[quote="Braithwhite"]
 &nbsp;You are GOING to get sedative flechetted at some point.&nbsp;  
[/quote]


&nbsp;

 Fun fact: &nbsp;It&#39;s actually possible to win this without seeing the Sedative Fletchettes even once! 

&nbsp;

 Doing so (at least the path I used, there might be others) pretty much requires exact knowledge of the villain and environment decks and several non-intuitive tactics, but it can be done. 

&nbsp;

 Details below in white 

[color=white]Round 1: &nbsp;Visionary plays Prophetic Visions and puts Pillars of Hercules (yes, really) on top. &nbsp;Visonary passes her power draw to Legacy. &nbsp;Legacy plays Inspiring Presence. &nbsp;Do not deal enough damage to destroy the components. &nbsp;You really don&#39;t want Cosmitron chaining drones with Pillars of Hercules out. [/color] <br /><br /> [color=white]  Round 2: &nbsp;Leave Pillars out. &nbsp;They&#39;ll play a few drones, but it won&#39;t be too bad. &nbsp;Don&#39;t play the second Prophetic Visions. &nbsp;Pass your power draw to Legacy again. &nbsp;Legacy will play Bolster Allies and draw Take Down, which she will then play. &nbsp;You can destroy all of Cosmitron&#39;s components now - there won&#39;t be any drone chaining ever again. &nbsp;Wail on the evil robot as much as you can.  [/color] <br /><br /> [color=white]  Round 3: Play Prophetic Visions to dodge the Seaweed and the Leaking Room. &nbsp;Use Suggestion to put a component on top of Cosmitron&#39;s deck. &nbsp;Start blowing up the Adaptive Platings. &nbsp;Legacy should skip her turn to destroy Pillars of Hercules. &nbsp;This will preserve Take Down for another round. &nbsp;Continue wailing on Cosmitron.  [/color] <br /><br /> [color=white]  Round 4: More wailing.  [/color] <br /><br /> [color=white]  Round 5: Kill Cosmitron.[/color]
